//api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/71507","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71507","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71507.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71507.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nListing Dags restricts the results to the Dag IDs the user may read. That permitted set is repeated as a predicate across the main query, the latest-run subquery, the pagination filters and the count query, and building it asks the auth manager for a decision on every Dag in the deployment. Both costs grow with the number of Dags even when the user is authorized on all of them, and the Dag list page pays them on each request it fires.\n\nAn auth manager can now declare that its Dag decisions do not depend on the Dag ID. Airflow then drops the predicate and stops authorizing Dags one at a time. The hook defaults to `False`, so an auth manager that does not opt in keeps today's behavior. FAB already had this answer and was discarding it; `SimpleAuthManager` opts in for admins, whose access does not depend on the Dag's team.\n\nThis does not fix the latency reported in #71499. That comes from per-Dag authorization requests in the Keycloak auth manager, which needs an upstream batch API, and Keycloak does not opt in to this hook.\n\n## Change\n\nOnly `PermittedDagFilter` drops its predicate. `dag_run`, `backfill`, `dag_warning` and `log` have no cascading foreign key to `dag`, so their rows can outlive the Dag they name and the predicate is what keeps those leftovers hidden — the subclasses keep filtering. The filter still exposes the full permitted set, so the routes that read it directly are untouched and cannot fail open, which is also why the enumeration itself stays.\n\n`is_authorized_all_dags` is evaluated twice per Dag-listing request, once in the filter dependency and once inside `get_authorized_dag_ids`. Both built-in implementations answer from memory.\n\n## Behavior change\n\nNone: both paths change only for an auth manager that declares its decisions independent of the Dag ID.\n\nRelated: #71499\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [x] Yes — Claude Code (Opus 5)\n\nGenerated-by: Claude Code (Opus 5) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/71507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/71507/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":29521657359,"node_id":"SE_lADOAgUK288AAAABMdUR9s8AAAAG36C-Dw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/29521657359","actor":{"login":"tirkarthi","id":3972343,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NzIzNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3972343?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tirkarthi","html_url":"https://github.com/tirkarthi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tirkarthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tirkarthi/following{/other_user}","gists